course: dictionary
lesson: 9734
title: Sunlit and the power of a picture word
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words paint a picture in just one word. «Sunlit» is built from two parts: sun and lit. Lit means given light, so sunlit means lit by the sun, bright with sunshine. Writers use it to make a scene feel warm and cheerful: «a sunlit meadow» and «a sunlit room».
explain: Context shows you how the word works. «The stars are still in the sky during the day, but the bright sunlit sky hides them.» The sky is bright because of sunlight, so the stars cannot be seen. Ask yourself what the sentence would lose if you took the word out.
explain: In science, sunlit describes places that the Sun shines on. «The sunlit zone is the top 200 metres of the ocean, where there is enough light for plant-like plankton to grow.» Here sunlit names a real layer of the sea, not just a nice mood. Its opposites are shady, dark and moonlit.
fact: Sunlit means lit by the sun, bright with sunshine.
fact: «A sunlit meadow» and «a sunlit room» are bright, warm and cheerful pictures.
fact: «The sunlit zone» is the top 200 metres of the ocean, where there is enough light for plankton to grow.
fact: «Moonlit» and «shady» are opposites of sunlit: moonlit means lit by the Moon, and shady means out of the sun.
fact: The Moon's phases happen because we see different amounts of its sunlit half as it orbits the Earth.
exercise: «The sunlit meadow was full of buttercups.» What does sunlit mean? | Dark and damp under the trees | *Lit by the sun, bright with sunshine | Covered in snow | Very windy and cold
exercise: Find and copy the word in «the bright sunlit sky hides them» that is closest in meaning to sunlit. | them | sky | hides | *bright
exercise: Where is the sunlit zone in the ocean? | *The top 200 metres, where sunlight reaches | In the rivers that flow into the sea | The deepest black floor, where no light gets in | Under the sand on the beach
test: «The Moon's phases happen because we see different amounts of its sunlit half.» What does sunlit half mean? | The half covered in clouds | *The half lit by the Sun | The half made of water | The half that is always hidden under shadow
test: Which word is the opposite of sunlit? | Cheerful | Warm | *Shady | Bright
exam: Which picture would a writer describe as «a sunlit meadow»? | *A field full of flowers on a bright, warm afternoon | A dark street at midnight | A stormy sea under heavy clouds | A cave with no light at all
